              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_29_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.414,
            0.884,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We need to identify only one more point to make this a 4-sided figure. That point, let us call it D, should be 5 cm from both B and C. How can such a point be found?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.482,
            0.786,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can any of the ideas used in the ‘House’ problem be used here?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.539,
            0.63,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.585,
            0.884,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All the points of a circle are at the same distance from its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "centre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This distance is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "radius",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the circle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.631,
            0.779,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "■ A compass can be used to construct circles and their parts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.654,
            0.884,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "■ A rough diagram can be useful in planning how to construct a given figure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.699,
            0.885,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "■ A rectangle can be constructed given the lengths of its sides or that of one of its sides and a diagonal."
            }
          ]
        },
